import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Technical" description="Current technical specification of the Voltii EV conversion">
  <h1>Technical Overview</h1>
  <p><em>A living summary — updated as decisions are finalised. See the journal for the reasoning behind each one.</em></p>

  <h2>Powertrain</h2>
  <p>
    Nissan Leaf EM57 motor and inverter (80kW/250Nm standard unit), full transaxle
    delete via a coupler onto the raw output shaft. Drive
    goes into a retained Getrag 245/4 four-speed gearbox through an
    adapter. The BMW diff is the sole reduction stage, targeting 4.10:1.
  </p>

  <h2>Brakes</h2>
  <p>
    Bosch iBooster using factory RHD-specific part numbers (Tesla-platform sourced),
    replacing the original remote servo. CAN-free: 12V ignition-switched power, 12V
    battery, ground only.
  </p>

  <h2>Battery, BMS &amp; Controller</h2>
  <p>
    Still open. Targeting 30–40kWh, weighing reused Leaf modules against new EVE
    prismatic LFP cells. Leaning toward an openinverter/Zombieverter controller with
    an Orion Jr2 or REC BMS.
  </p>

  <h2>Compliance</h2>
  <p>
    Queensland NCOP LV1 pathway, via a local TMR signatory engaged for sign-off.
  </p>

  <p><a href="/journal">&larr; Back to the journal</a></p>
</BaseLayout>
